# Copy standard input to standard output, byte for byte.
# langlib original.
#
# Usage: echo -n meow | lake exe unlambda Langlib/Examples/Unlambda/cat.unl
#
# @ reads a byte and applies its argument to i on success or to v at end
# of input; | hands the byte back as a printing function. The loop is a
# function applied to itself, and the recursive call sits inside a `d
# promise so that it is not evaluated until the i case forces it. Give
# the v case that promise instead and nothing happens, because v
# swallows whatever it is applied to: that is the whole conditional.
````s`k`s`k@``s``s`ks``s`k`s`ks``s`k`s`k`si``s`k`s`k`s`kd``s`k`s`k`s``s`k|`k``si`ki``s``s`ks``s`k`s`ks``s``s`ks``s`k`s`ks``s`k`s`kkk``s`k`s`kkk`k`k`ki`k`k`ki``s`k`s`k@``s``s`ks``s`k`s`ks``s`k`s`k`si``s`k`s`k`s`kd``s`k`s`k`s``s`k|`k``si`ki``s``s`ks``s`k`s`ks``s``s`ks``s`k`s`ks``s`k`s`kkk``s`k`s`kkk`k`k`ki`k`k`kii
